{{Quote|Each of us has light within us. Our job as Jedi is to help each other find that light, so we can then share it with others.|Jedi Master Zia Zaldor Zanna, to Jedi Initiates Kai Brighstar and [[Djovi Resmia]]|<ref name="Clash">{{YJA|Clash}}</ref>}}
'''Zia Zaldor Zanna''' was a [[Jedi Master]] stationed on the [[planet]] [[Tenoo]] to teach [[Jedi Initiate]]s during the [[High Republic Era]].

==Biography==
===Early life===
During her [[Jedi training|training]] on [[Rex Strata]],<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> Zia Zaldor Zanna befriended a [[Houk]] [[technician]] [[Faraz]], at some point wrecking one of his [[speeder]]s, and became rivals with the [[Pirate|thief]] [[Ace Kallisto]]. However, the rivalry would turn into more of a friendly squabble as Zanna grew older.<ref name="The Jedi and the Thief" />

When she was younger, Zanna was stationed at the [[Tenoo Jedi Temple]], an outpost temple in the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]. She met the [[Guardian of the Tenoo Jedi Temple]], a large [[tazi sloth]] that lived in the canopy of the giant [[Tenoo tree]] that the temple was built around.<ref name="Rainy Day Beast">{{YJA |The Rainy Day Beast}}</ref>

===Stationed on Tenoo===
{{Quote|I'm so proud of you. Helping people is what Jedi do.|Jedi Master Zia Zaldor Zanna, to the Jedi Initiates|<ref name="TYJ">{{YJA|The Young Jedi}}</ref>}}
[[File:ZiaZaldorZanna-CGSWG.png|thumb|left|250px|Zia Zaldor Zanna was a Jedi Master by 233 BBY.]]
[[Standard year|Years]] later around [[233 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{YJADate|101A}}</ref> Zanna, now a [[Jedi Master]], along with other [[Jedi]] was in the [[Jedi Temple training ground|training ground]] of the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on [[Coruscant]] when [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] announced that [[Jedi Initiate]]s would be sent to an [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[Tenoo Jedi Temple|outpost temple]] for further training. As most of the Jedi left, Zanna's [[droid]] [[Dee]] noted that some of the [[youngling]]s were missing. Zanna laughed and easily guessed that [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]], [[Nubs]] were the last missing [[Jedi Initiate|Initiates]]. Zanna soon told them to get to the last [[shuttle]] ''[[Crimson Firehawk]]'' via a [[holoprojector]].<ref name="TYJ" />

Master Zanna once supervised a class where Brightstar, Solay and Nubs undertook an obstacle course involving [[DD-1 hover droid]]s. During the exercise, Brightstar tried to [[Telekinesis|levitate]] both [[Kai's first lightsaber|his training lightsaber]] and cushion Nub's fall. Though he was able to retrieve his lightsaber, he was unable to stop Nubs from falling. Zanna subsequently terminated the exercise. Though Nubs was unhurt, the younglings failed the objective: reaching the platform together. After the visiting Yoda counselled the younglings to work as a team, Zanna sent them on a mission with Yoda and their pilot friend [[Nash Durango]] to retrieve [[Sparkle-fire seed]]s.<ref name="Yoda's Mission">{{YJA|Yoda's Mission}}</ref>

===Blast from the past===
====Old friends====
Sometime later, Zanna was planning on going to meet Faraz on Rex Strata to trade for a [[cryo-spanner]] to repair the [[Tenoo Jedi Temple|Jedi Temple's]] [[cooling unit]]. However, she noticed that Brightstar made fun of the pirate [[Cyrus Vuundir|Taborr Val Dorn]] with a make-shift [[helmet]]. Zanna decided to invite Brightstar along for her mission to get the cryo-spanner. As they arrived on the [[planet]], Zanna introduced Brightstar to her old friend Faraz. Faraz and Zanna traded for the cryo-spanner and reminisced on their past, but the discussion was cut short after Brightstar notified her that their [[shuttle]] was stolen.<ref name="The Jedi and the Thief" />

Zanna and Brightstar quickly took Faraz's [[speeder bike]] to chase after their shuttle. They then made a daring [[Force jump|jump]] from the speeder bike to the top of the shuttle, though the speeder exploded after they jumped off. Entering the shuttle and into the [[cockpit]], it was Kallisto who hijacked their shuttle. Kallisto told the Jedi that their shuttle sold well. Brightstar drew his [[Brightstar's second lightsaber|lightsaber]] to protect Zanna but accidentally damaged the ship with it. The damage caused the shuttle to crash into a [[cave]] nearby. As they got up from the crash, Zanna's [[Limb|ankle]] was injured in the process, and she was unable to move.<ref name="The Jedi and the Thief" />

====The crash====
They noticed that the [[Unidentified cave (Stalaat)|cave]] they crashed into was not an empty cave, but rather a home of a [[stalaat]]. With Zanna's ankle injured during the crash, she used it as an opportunity to teach Brightstar a lesson about the choice to do good and tasked him to work with Kallisto. Brightstar and Kallisto then went out of the shuttle to [[Distress signal|signal]] for help. Another stalaat quickly jumped in and startled Brightstar and Kallisto. Seeing an opportunity, Kallisto returned to the ship and used the armaments of the ship to scare the stalaats away with Zanna. Brightstar used the [[comlink]] and called for help.<ref name="The Jedi and the Thief" />

Soon, backup arrived to assist Zanna and the others. As [[DUM-series pit droid]]s repaired the shuttle, an [[AZ-series surgical assistant droid]] used [[bacta spray]] on Zanna's injured ankle. Zanna and Kallisto sat down and reminisced for a bit before leaving. Zanna later approached Brightstar and seeing that he had learnt his lesson, they went back to the Jedi Temple on Tenoo. Brightstar quickly removed the make-shift helmet from the training droid and continued training with Nubs and Solay.<ref name="The Jedi and the Thief" />

===Mentor and guardian===
Zanna later helped the pilot Durango to organize a concert thanking the Jedi for helping [[Kublop Springs]]. She helped three younglings, who had tripped while hoisting a curtain in the theatre.<ref name="TSMGO">{{YJA|The Show Must Go On}}</ref> Later, Zanna comforted Brightstar who was upset after he slept in and missed a field trip to the [[Lava fields (Tiss'ell)|lava fields]] of [[Tiss'ell]]. She reassured the youngling that everyone experienced "bad day" and sent him on an errand with Durango to deliver a [[hyperdrive]] capacitator to the [[hyperspace]] prospector [[Mycho Zala]].<ref name="KBD">{{YJA|Kai's Bad Day}}</ref>

Zanna later organized [[Visitor's Day]] in Kublop Springs for the benefit of offworld visitors to Tenoo. One of the exhibits on display was the [[Chadra-Fan]] junkyard dealer [[Marlaa Jinara]]'s [[Visitor's Day sculpture]]. The unscrupulous [[Moldwarp]] art dealer [[Draiven Bosh]] distracted Zanna while his two droids [[K-2PL]] and [[R4-13]] stole the sculpture and brought it aboard [[Draiven Bosh's shuttle|his starship]]. The younglings Brightstar, Solay and Nubs pursued the thieves aboard Bosh's ship but were trapped by the dealer. Solay managed to contact Zanna, who was able to track down their comm signal.<ref name="Visitor's Day">{{YJA|Visitor's Day (episode)}}</ref> 

The younglings distracted Bosh until Zanna arrived and forced her aboard Bosh's starship. Zanna demanded that Bosh return the Visitor's Day sculpture and other stolen artifacts but he refused. Acting under Bosh's orders, K-2PL attempted to drive the Jedi out of Bosh's starship by tilting the ship outward. However, he ended up causing Bosh's stolen crates to fall out of the starship with the Jedi. The Jedi used their Force powers to cushion their wall and retrieve the Visitor's Day sculpture and other stolen artifacts. While Solay was upset that Bosh had escaped, Zanna was relieved that they had recovered the stolen artifacts and tasked the younglings with returning them to their owners.<ref name="Visitor's Day" />

While Zanna was away, Nubs accidentally brought back the seeds of an aggressive [[grumble vine]], which almost took over the Tenoo temple. Working together, the Jedi younglings managed to subdue the threat. After returning, Nubs chatted with the [[alien]] botanist [[Varish]], who apologized for accidentally giving Nubs the grumble vines seeds after mistaking them for another plant. She credited Nubs for using his lesson of observation to subdue the aggressive plant.<ref name="TGGD">{{YJA|The Growing Green Danger}}</ref> When Master [[Loden Greatstorm]] and his Padawan [[Bell Zettifar]] visited the Tenoo temple, Zanna took Greatstorm on a tour of the temple with Solay and Nubs. Brightstar meanwhile befriended Zettifar and his pet [[charhound]] [[Ember]] and took them on a tour of the surrounding forest.<ref name="Charhound Chase">{{YJA|Charhound Chase}}</ref>

Later, Master Zia supervised a lightsaber sparring class. She paired Brightstar with another ambitious Jedi youngling named [[Djovi Resmia]], who defeated him in a sparring exercise. Brightstar, who was used to winning, was upset about losing the match. Concerned about potential rivalry between the two younglings, Zanna tasked the dour with retrieving a damaged [[beacon stone]] from the rope path bridge on a nearby Tenoo tree. Despite their initial hostility and rivalry, the two younglings mended their differences and became friends after working together to retrieve the beacon stone from a chasm. Resmia was able to make peace with his jealousy of Brightstar's abilities while Brightstar thanked Resmia for saving his life. Following their mission, Zanna repaired the damaged beacon stone with her lightsaber, causing it to shine again. She used this lesson to teach the Jedi about the importance of finding the light in others. Satisfied that they had learned the importance of teamwork, Zanna tasked them with returning the beacon stone to its place.<ref name="Clash">{{YJA|Clash}}</ref>

Zanna later accompanied the Jedi younglings to the windy planet [[Kondoraan]], which was home to giant [[broadleaf tree]]s. She and the younglings visited a floating platform where a [[Nautolan]] instructor named [[Rix Tegano]] taught the younglings about [[sky skimming]]. Zanna explained that the people of Kondoraan used giant leaves known as [[sky skimming board]]s to travel around the windy planet. She added that it was important for Jedi to learn about other cultures. During the lesson, the younglings Brightstar, Nubs and Solay got lost after they were blown offcourse while trying to follow a flock of [[chiffon]]s. After landing in the desert, the trio worked together to use their cloaks as improvised sails and rejoined the others. Zanna was relieved that the three younglings were safe and well. Brightstar said that the trio learned about the importance of following the wind.<ref name="TGLG">{{YJA|The Great Leaf Glide}}</ref>
{{Char-stub}}

==Personality and traits==
Zanna was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[human]] with [[Color|black]] [[hair]], green [[Eye|eyes]], and tan skin.<ref name="Encyclopedia" />

She was wise, kind, patient, and gentle with the younglings she instructed.<ref name="TYJ" /> She had a childhood rivalry with the pirate, Ace Kallisto, but as they both grew older she came to realize that Kallisto wasn't all bad.<ref name="The Jedi and the Thief" /> A realization that would lead her to a life&ndash;long<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> belief that people who do bad things could later make the choice to do good.<ref name="The Jedi and the Thief" />

